  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Reachable without an inbound port",
      "items": [
        "A worker behind NAT opens no listening port: one outbound connection carries every stream",
        "The relay binds loopback only, so adding nodes adds no public surface",
        "The address stays an ordinary host and port, so the transport can be swapped without touching the request path"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Identity decides before address does",
      "items": [
        "Four layers: an offline root authorises signers, signers issue node credentials, each node holds one key, sessions use an in-memory key",
        "Whether a node may join is verified on the node itself, so a compromised control plane cannot silently insert one",
        "Anything unverifiable is refused with a named reason — never a silent fall back to a shared credential or default host"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Direct is an optimisation, never a requirement",
      "items": [
        "Candidate endpoints ride the connection that already exists, so the direct path adds no port and no protocol",
        "A direct path counts only when both directions work; otherwise it falls back by name — off, cooling down, no address, one-way, past the deadline",
        "Switching it off is not a loss of function: joining and admission still work, the traffic keeps going through the relay"
      ]
    }
  ]
